rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Runtime-native workflows must comply with the CAS Workflow Execution Model,
    maintaining separation of concerns where CAS Runner orchestrates, workflows reason,
    and knowledge providers manage access.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity levels and decision
    statuses to prevent conflating knowledge evolution with governance validation.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All new patterns must be created as 'supporting' by default and validated
    through evidence and usage before being considered for 'core' status.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the consolidation or merging of patterns across different architectural
    layers to maintain clarity between governance, execution, contracts, and reliability.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to 'core' status must be supported by strong, observable
    evidence from multiple sources or system contexts to ensure foundational stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for architectural planning;
    all generated artifacts must derive planning status from it rather than maintaining
    independent state.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates the use of a structured YAML decision schema for all Architecture
    Decision Records (ADR) to enable machine processing and consistent interpretation.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared knowledge workspace and are prohibited
    from duplicating workspace-level governance structures or established global directories.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the semantic contract for architectural artifacts, distinguishing
    between intent and state, and architect decisions versus governance-approved system
    state.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns derived from heuristics must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure traceability and grounded insights.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes the system-wide hierarchy for conflict resolution where Global
    Rules override Project Rules, and Project Rules override Prompt Rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be proposed by the system and explicitly
    accepted, rejected, or deferred by a human architect to maintain control.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts like AEM and AID must summarize data from
    authoritative sources and cannot serve as authoritative sources themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in ADR files;
    all other system representations must be derived from these records.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: "Defines mandatory criteria\u2014recurrence, system impact, reusability,\
    \ and stability\u2014that a signal must satisfy before being promoted to a pattern."
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR files before
    they can be reflected in mapping artifacts or system state representations.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item must be derived from its decision
    status; items not explicitly 'accepted' cannot be marked as 'DONE'.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) must remain consistent with Architecture
    Decision Records (ADR) and is prohibited from contradicting them.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns are restricted to foundational architectural primitives;
    context-specific strategies or implementations must not be promoted to the core.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
